It seems to me more like a variation on the
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broken_window_fallacy

Suppose I jump 2.5 squares per turn, and you (very fast) walk 1.667 
squares per turn, and the no-tele level has 25 squares to cross.  It 
takes you 15 turns, during which you gain 15d4 mana.  It takes me ten 
turns, so I gain only 10d4 mana... but I'm five turns ahead of you.  No 
matter what I spend those five turns doing (and it will certainly be 
something better than 'n5s'), I'll gain 5d4 mana, making us even in that 
respect.  

